{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"x0x","displayName":"x0x","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/jimcollinson/skills/x0x","publisherHandle":"jimcollinson","publisherDisplayName":"Jim Collinson","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/jimcollinson","version":"0.48.1","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1792301029729,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/x0x/card?ownerHandle=jimcollinson&version=0.48.1","sha256":"78b854b84d9dc7dc07202ee3a511c001149468fc62acfb37f339065b1d8f00b0","size":2489,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"5e63c480164fc9587a9f8185b34e0da8be2ceef7e05c66ff4acf92a665e3dae0","bundleFingerprints":["1493e8c5f6216cdf9a47f0aad1ebb0de059b8940f15d9326bc8628b7e68d4a6c"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":29490,"sha256":"6875510c1d3a6d0b4b6a3080a4c348cc8960b2fb89bd4347d6bada9dcc833432","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill is mostly coherent for an agent networking daemon, but it deserves Review because it combines persistent installation, bearer-token daemon control, remote execution, and self-update authority.","model":null,"checkedAt":1792301695759,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.2","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[],"properties":{"securityScore":100,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1792301631.603005,"endTime":1792301642.9813154}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"x0x","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57ez3fv5h89sbxenjmpb2gpex8ggfbq-3uNYKn/clawscan-skillspector-1498705088/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-10-18T05:33:51.047397+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":63,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":390,"executable":false,"size_bytes":29490,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-bb0ddec09acf475ba1fd278a2dbac567","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":278,"end_line":null},"finding":"DELETE /sync/devices/:machine_id","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"```bash\nx0x sync enroll                    # POST /sync/devices/enroll {} — owner-key-sign a DeviceEnrollment for THIS machine\nx0x sync devices                   # GET /sync/devices — enrolled devices + last-sync status\nx0x sync revoke <machine_id>       # DELETE /sync/devices/:machine_id — next stream from it is refused\n```\n\n- **Tier 1 — replicates today:** exactly four record kinds — owner profile, per-machine agent/machine names, the Home roster + policy pointer, and the sub-agent issuance journal (small signed state-commits over the sync stream; last-writer-wins by commit height).","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"db83b2077bedbf90af6b8661452bec9e455d22033bf83b644839d1a7de83db42","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":278,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA1","finding_id":"finding-29bd9ae876254f07a3601fbe2363dc2e","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Self-Modification","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":349,"end_line":null},"finding":"Self-update","explanation":"The documented self-update capability (`POST /upgrade/apply`) enables the software to replace or modify its own installed binaries. In an agent skill context, self-update materially increases risk because a compromised daemon, stolen bearer token, or malicious instruction chain could trigger code changes and persistence without a separate trusted package-management flow.","remediation":"Gate self-update behind explicit human approval and out-of-band verification. Require signed, pinned updates with integrity checks, disable automatic apply by default in agent-facing workflows, and restrict or remove upgrade endpoints from skills unless absolutely necessary.","code_snippet":"| Voice 1:1 (datagram + fallback) | library (`voice` feature) | `--example voice_call` | GA (lib) · 2nd concurrent call refused (typed `SessionConflict` via `start_lane`; `IoError`-wrapped via trait `start()`) |\n| Diagnostics (11 areas) | `/diagnostics/*` | `x0x diagnostics <area>` | GA |\n| Durable history | `/history*` | `x0x history scopes/list/message/search/stats/purge` | GA (local-only; Tier-2 Home backfill designed, not shipped — [Stores, files, and history](https://github.com/saorsa-labs/x0x/blob/main/docs/skill/stores.md) §4.10, §5.1) |\n| Self-update | daemon: `/upgrade(+/apply)` · CLI: read-only check | `x0x upgrade --check`; authenticated `POST /upgrade/apply` to install | GA |\n\n---\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"bd002ac10f47a5ff8b5acbe18edb9cf06dba73d787e329e8585d8f7a24c528d9","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":349,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-3d7c89a8ad7e43c09e03800caf23762a","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":121,"end_line":null},"finding":"mkdir -p ~/.local/bin\ncp \"x0x-${PLATFORM}/x0xd\" \"x0x-${PLATFORM}/x0x\" ~/.local/bin/ && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/x0xd ~/.local/bin/x0x\n```\n\n**Option B: shell installer (installs and starts the daemon)** —","explanation":"The installation instructions copy executables into `~/.local/bin`, creating persistent user-level tooling that can later be invoked by the agent or user. Persistence alone is not always malicious, but in a skill context it expands long-term attack surface, especially because the binaries are downloaded from the network and installed outside a package manager with no integrity verification shown in Option A.","remediation":"Prefer non-persistent execution or installation through a trusted package manager. If local installation is necessary, require checksum/signature verification, install into a versioned application directory, and ask for explicit human confirmation before modifying persistent PATH-accessible locations.","code_snippet":"  *) printf 'Unsupported platform: %s-%s\\n' \"$OS\" \"$ARCH\" >&2; exit 1 ;;\nesac\ncurl -sfL \"https://github.com/saorsa-labs/x0x/releases/latest/download/x0x-${PLATFORM}.tar.gz\" | tar xz\nmkdir -p ~/.local/bin\ncp \"x0x-${PLATFORM}/x0xd\" \"x0x-${PLATFORM}/x0x\" ~/.local/bin/ && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/x0xd ~/.local/bin/x0x\n```\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"63751746887fecef86ff13dee74c9ced5e84553c580e98f3a62b006dcc8edb02","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":121,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-b3d6e139c8f74f9494fa913c4818fe69","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":128,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -sfLO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/saorsa-labs/x0x/main/scripts/install.sh\nless install.sh && sh install.sh\n```\n\nThe separate [`scripts/install.py`](https://github.com/saorsa-labs/x0x/blob/m","explanation":"The skill explicitly instructs downloading and executing a remote shell script with `sh install.sh`. Even though it says to review the script first, this still creates a high-risk supply-chain path because the script is fetched from a mutable branch URL and the document admits it does not verify GPG signatures, while also starting/stopping daemons automatically.","remediation":"Remove direct execution guidance for unsigned remote scripts. Replace this path with a pinned, checksum- or signature-verified installer, or require using the prebuilt release artifacts with published hashes/signatures. If a script installer must exist, pin to an immutable release URL/commit, verify integrity before execution, and separate install from daemon startup by default.","code_snippet":"**Option B: shell installer (installs and starts the daemon)** — download and review the script before running it. It downloads over HTTPS but does **not** verify GPG signatures. It stops the selected existing instance and starts the installed daemon automatically; `--autostart` additionally enables startup on boot. There is no `--start` opt-in. Run this option only when your human has authorized the install and daemon startup. To install the binaries before starting a daemon, use Option A and follow §1.2 when authorized.\n\n```bash\ncurl -sfLO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/saorsa-labs/x0x/main/scripts/install.sh\nless install.sh && sh install.sh\n```\n","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"debed5736fcfc652119828ec030b0fd0faf05f867b05b8cdc57217e43f0e31de","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":128,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-97a82dc190e744b89491c42a6850ce65","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":190,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -N -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \"http://$API/events\"     # SSE; fields nested under \"data\"\n```\n\nTopics starting `local:` are never gossipped — same-daemon IPC only.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Identity Mode","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"curl -X POST \"http://$API/subscribe\" -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"topic\":\"hello-world\"}'\ncurl -X POST \"http://$API/publish\"   -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"topic\":\"hello-world\",\"payload\":\"'$(echo -n \"Hello!\" | base64 | tr -d '\\n')'\"}'   # tr -d '\\n': BOTH GNU and BSD base64 wrap long output at 76 cols — unwrapped it breaks the JSON\ncurl -N -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \"http://$API/events\"     # SSE; fields nested under \"data\"\n```\n\nTopics starting `local:` are never gossipped — same-daemon IPC only.","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c211ad589101c1dd98d0f833ec371ce94fac7b51b8febde2ba83e81a6f3679c8","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":190,"end_line":null}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":10451,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":9984,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":10465},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":10500,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":9984,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":10514},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_s